{
  "_comment": "Golden parity fixtures for the deterministic planner pipeline (parse -> normalize -> apply_defaults -> validate). Consumed by BOTH the Python (python/core/tests/test_planner_parity.py) and Rust (knaif-core planner parity test) validators; both must produce the same valid/invalid outcome + error substring. Registries are inline tools.yaml text so parity is on an identical registry, independent of skill content.",
  "registries": {
    "demo": "find:\n  description: Find files\n  required_args: [path]\n  optional_args: [file_type]\ncompress:\n  description: Compress\n  required_args: [input]\n  optional_args: [quality, output, tries, at]\n  defaults: {output: out.mp4}\n  arg_schemas:\n    quality: {type: enum, enum: [low, high], aliases: {maximum: high}}\n    tries: {type: integer, min: 1, max: 5}\n    at: {type: string}\ncombine:\n  description: Combine\n  optional_args: [inputs]\nreport:\n  description: Report\n  any_of_args: [a, b]\n  optional_args: [a, b]\nsecret_op:\n  description: Internal only\n  internal: true\n  required_args: [payload]\nstamp:\n  description: Stamp a file\n  required_args: [input]\n  arg_schemas:\n    output: {type: string}\n"
  },
