    {
      "name": "string_arg_given_as_a_number_is_coerced",
      "why": "A timestamp arg typed `string` must accept the model's bare number. ffmpeg's `start`/`end`/`duration` were untyped, so `{\"start\": 0, \"end\": 0}` reached Python's engine as ints and native's `str_arg` as None - one plan, two different rendered commands. Typing them fixed it only because both runtimes coerce here identically, which is what this pins.",
      "registry": "demo",
